    "text": "To determine how many mph above the speed limit John was driving, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate John's actual speed.\n2. Determine the difference between John's speed and the speed limit.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate John's actual speed.**\n\nJohn travels 150 miles in 2 hours. The formula for speed is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Speed} = \\frac{150 \\text{ miles}}{2 \\text{ hours}} = 75 \\text{ mph}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine how many mph above the speed limit John was driving.**\n\nThe speed limit is 60 mph. John's actual speed is 75 mph. The difference between John's speed and the speed limit is:\n\n\\[\n75 \\text{ mph} - 60 \\text{ mph} = 15 \\text{ mph}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, John was driving \\(\\boxed{15}\\) mph above the speed limit.",
